A||||0||Rodrv6||A Different Sort of Clutch Problem (kinda long)||||4||
Z||000000||Rodrv6||08-20-2001||09:35 PM||||Last Wednesday evening while driving home in my 88 GT the clutch started acting strange.  It felt spongy all of a sudden just like there was air in the system.  It would barely disengage with the pedal all the way to the floor, and the pedal felt very soft.  I got the car home, but couldn't do anything until Saturday evening.  I had replaced the slave cylinder about 1 month ago so I was sure it was fine.  I checked the boot around the pedal pushrod on the master cylinder and it was full of fluid. Aha!!  So I put a new master cylinder on it this afternoon and bled it until I was blue in the face, but the pedal was still soft like there was air somewhere.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I finally concluded that something must be wrong with the clutch itself, so I began removing the engine. (I've dropped several 4 cylinders, but this was my first V6.)  I've found it easier for me just to take the whole powertrain out at once and separate the transmission with the engine still attatched to the cradle.  Took 3 hours and 45 minutes to get to the problem.  I found that about half the diameter of the clutch lining on the pressure plate side had disintegrated and fallen off of the disc! That explains the strange feel.  I'll buy a new clutch tomorrow and hopefully get the car back together Wednesday or Thursday if all goes well.<BR>I've seen some previous postings regarding clutches that didn't seem to bleed properly.  If anyone else has these symptoms and all else fails it might be worth checking the clutch itself. <P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||4
